# Neo Desktop Calendar Permissions

## Roles

| Role | Meaning |
| --- | --- |
| `super_admin` | Full store + admin settings (members, security, holidays API, backup) |
| `member` | Own calendars/events + holidays-kr view; no admin surfaces |
| (guest) | Not logged in — empty projected store; login required to edit |

Legacy stored role `admin` normalizes to `super_admin`.

Session `AuthUser.role` must come from `members.json` (not a hardcoded `'admin'`).

## Capabilities (`can(user, capability)`)

Super admin only:

- `manageMembers`
- `manageMemberCalendars`
- `manageSecurity`
- `manageWebServer`
- `syncHolidays`
- `backupStore`
- `importExportStore`

UI gates are not enough — enforce the same checks in IPC (`main.ts`) and HTTP (`apiRouter` / `browserFileRoutes`).

## Data projection

`CalendarStore.getSnapshotForLogin(loginId, surface, isSuperAdmin)`:

- Guest: empty calendars/events/tags
- Super admin: full store (+ per-login eye-toggle / dayColors projection)
- Member: personal calendars/events + `holidays-kr` only; strip API keys / IP allowlists

Prefer passing `isSuperAdmin` from `AuthUser.role === 'super_admin'` rather than comparing env admin id alone.

## Member UX

Members keep: 일반, 내 계정(비밀번호), 새 캘린더, 태그, 내/고정 캘린더 설정, 검색·일정 편집·Excel/PDF/HTML 내보내기(본인 스냅샷).

Members lose: 가져오기/내보내기(전체), 보안, 서버 관리, 회원 관리, 회원 캘린더 관리, 공휴일 API 동기화.
